# The claim that a set with an operation forms a group: closure, associativity, a two-sided identity, and a two-sided
# inverse for every element. The finite-group instances whose orders are machine-checked (the binary tetrahedral group
# of order twenty-four, the Weyl group of F4 of order one thousand one hundred fifty-two) live in the group files; this
# note records the group axioms a structural claim verifies.
